.\" restate-proxy's manual page, written by hand: restate-proxy has a dozen
.\" options and no generated help to build it from. scripts/check-proxy-man.sh
.\" (part of make lint) fails if an option `restate-proxy --help` lists is not
.\" here, so it cannot fall behind. docs/proxy-protocol.md is the whole story.
.\"
.\" Copyright (c) 2026 Bryan C. Everly
.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.TH RESTATE-PROXY 8 "November 10, 2026" "restate-proxy" "System Manager's Manual"
.nh
.SH NAME
restate-proxy \- serve restate repositories over HTTPS, append-only
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B restate-proxy
.B \-\-serve
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR HOST:PORT ]...
.RB [ \-\-cert
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-grants
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-connections
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-idle\-timeout
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-sessions
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-lease
.IR SECONDS ]
.RB [ \-\-staging
.IR DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-staging
.IR MIB ]
.br
.B restate-proxy
.B \-\-check\-grants
.RI [ DIR ]
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.br
.B restate-proxy
.B \-\-new\-token
.I FILE
.br
.B restate-proxy
.BR \-\-version " | " \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B restate-proxy
runs on the machine that stores
.BR restate (8)
repositories, and lets the machines that capture into them reach them over
HTTPS without being able to remove or change what is there. A client may
add a snapshot, and read, list and restore what its grant allows; nothing it
sends can take anything out of a repository. A capture cut off part way
leaves nothing of itself behind once its session ends.
.PP
restate reaches a repository behind the proxy by its URL,
.IR https://HOST:PORT/v1/CLIENT ,
with
.B \-\-repository\-token\-file
and, for a certificate the system does not trust,
.B \-\-repository\-ca\-file
or
.BR \-\-repository\-pin\-sha256 .
.PP
Each connection is served by a process of its own, confined as tightly as
the system allows: Landlock and seccomp on Linux,
.BR pledge (2)
and
.BR unveil (2)
on OpenBSD, Capsicum on FreeBSD.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-serve
Serve the repositories the grants allow, until
.BR SIGTERM .
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " HOST:PORT"
Where to listen:
.I [ADDRESS]:PORT
for IPv6, or
.I :PORT
for every address. Repeatable; the default is
.BR :8443 .
.TP
.BI \-\-cert " FILE"
The certificate chain in PEM, the proxy's own certificate first
.RI ( /etc/restate/proxy.crt ).
Read once, at start.
.TP
.BI \-\-key " FILE"
Its private key in PEM, unencrypted
.RI ( /etc/restate/proxy.key ).
Read once, at start.
.TP
.BI \-\-grants " DIR"
The grants
.RI ( /etc/restate/proxy.d ),
read again on
.B SIGHUP
and whenever the directory changes.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-connections " N"
Connections served at once (64); one past it is closed as it comes.
.TP
.BI \-\-idle\-timeout " SECONDS"
How long a connection may say nothing before it is closed (60).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-sessions " N"
Sessions open at once (64); one past it is refused.
.TP
.BI \-\-lease " SECONDS"
How long a session lasts idle and unrenewed (300). restate renews its
session while it runs, and ends it as it finishes or is killed; a session
whose client vanished ends when its lease runs out.
.TP
.BI \-\-staging " DIR"
Where an append session's uploads wait to be committed
.RI ( /var/lib/restate-proxy/staging ).
Made if it is not there, its parent has to be; it has to be the proxy's
user's alone (mode 0700), or nothing can be uploaded.
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-staging " MIB"
The most one session's staging may hold (4096).
.TP
.BR \-\-check\-grants " [\fIDIR\fP]"
Read every grant in
.I DIR
.RI ( /etc/restate/proxy.d )
as the proxy would, and say what is wrong with each. Exit 2 if one is not
good.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Say it as JSON, schema 1.
.TP
.BI \-\-new\-token " FILE"
Write a new client token into
.IR FILE ,
which must not exist, readable only by its owner, and print the
.B token_sha256
line for the client's grant.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version, the protocol version and the TLS library.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print a summary of the options.
.SH GRANTS
A client's grant is a file in the grants directory named for it,
.IR CLIENT.conf ,
in restate's own
.I key = value
form. It is read only if it is root's or the proxy's user's and no one else
may write it, and a grant with an error grants nothing:
.PP
.RS
.nf
repository   = /srv/restate/web01
operations   = append, read
token_sha256 = 8f14e45fceea167a5a36dedd4bea2543c8d2d1e3c1b5d7d0a2a6a1f6c1f8a9e0
.fi
.RE
.PP
.B operations
is
.BR read ,
.BR append ,
or both.
A second
.B token_sha256
line lets a token be replaced without a run failing in between. Write a
grant under a name beginning with a dot and rename it into place: the proxy
reads only
.IR CLIENT.conf .
.PP
The repository is made with
.B restate init
and has to be the proxy's user's to write.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.B SIGHUP
Read the grants again.
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Stop listening, end every connection and every session, and exit 0.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/restate/proxy.d/
The grants, one per client.
.TP
.IR /etc/restate/proxy.crt ", " /etc/restate/proxy.key
The certificate chain and its key. Give the key to the proxy's user
alone: root's, its group the proxy's, mode 0640.
.TP
.I /var/lib/restate-proxy/staging/
Uploads waiting to be committed; what is there when the proxy starts is
removed.
.SH LOGGING
Standard error, a line per event in
.I key=value
form, which a service manager's journal keeps: what it listens on, the
grants it read and each it refused with why, each request, and each session
opened and ended. A token is never in it, nor a session's id.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Stopped by a signal, or the grants are all good.
.TP
.B 2
It could not start, or a grant is not good.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR restate (8)
.PP
The protocol, the grants and the confinement in full:
.I https://github.com/bceverly/restate/blob/main/docs/proxy-protocol.md
